<title>INDIA: India sugar prices rise on speculative purchases.</title>
<headline>India sugar prices rise on speculative purchases.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian sugar prices rose on Wednesday on speculative buying and less inflows though demand was low, dealers said.</p>
<p>In ready delivery sugar S-30 rose by 6/10 rupees to 1,315/1,331 rupees per quintal while M-30 gained by 10/19 rupees to 1,325/1,374 rupees. Sugar mill delivery rose to 1,240/1,250 rupees from 1,230/1,245 rupees on higher outstation buying.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
